Microcontroller firmware, not ROS packages. Keeps `colcon build` from
descending into this tree.

This file is load-bearing as of the move to PlatformIO. The old firmware/ held
nothing but .ino sketches, which colcon has no reason to look at -- but
teensy_drill_sys/extra_packages/rover_sensor_interfaces is a real ament_cmake
message package, complete with package.xml, and without this marker `colcon
list` finds it and `colcon build` starts building the rover's firmware
interfaces into the host workspace.

DO NOT put a COLCON_IGNORE inside teensy_drill_sys/extra_packages/ instead.
micro_ros_platformio copies that directory into its own build workspace and
runs colcon there, which is exactly how the custom message is meant to reach
the board -- an ignore marker inside it would be copied along and silently
drop the message from the firmware build.
